\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 1. Objective\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement a dedicated procedural engine that reconstructs the severe horizontal synchronization collapse, unstable luminance, and intermittent horizontal dropout behavior visible in 
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 video_1.mov
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 .\
The reference is dominated by rapidly changing horizontal bands, abrupt dark-to-bright luminance transitions, fragmented horizontal streaks, and subtle chromatic tint variations.\
This effect must have its own visual identity. Do not reduce it to a conventional tracking-noise preset, generic scanlines, or a combination of unrelated existing effects.\
The engine must generate the effect mathematically during rendering. Do not use pre-rendered textures, image overlays, GIFs, video layers, or baked animation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 2. Mandatory Existing-Project Audit\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Before implementation:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Inspect the complete VHSart project and its existing VHS DAMAGE LAB architecture.\
{\listtext	2.	}Locate existing tracking, sync, horizontal tear, dropout, luminance instability, signal noise, chroma, and temporal-processing components.\
{\listtext	3.	}Inspect their actual source implementations and determine which parts can be reused.\
{\listtext	4.	}Reuse shared low-level utilities where appropriate, including deterministic random generation, row-based sampling, compositing, and temporal evaluation.\
{\listtext	5.	}Do not duplicate existing functionality unnecessarily.\
{\listtext	6.	}Build a dedicated Sync Collapse & Luma Dropout Engine because the reference requires tightly coordinated horizontal geometry and abrupt luminance behavior that a generic preset may not reproduce accurately.\
{\listtext	7.	}Extend existing systems only where doing so preserves their original behavior.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Do not replace, remove, or break existing VHSart engines or presets.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 3. Reference Visual Characteristics\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Reproduce the following visual properties:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Severe horizontal banding across the full frame.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Alternating bright, medium-gray, and nearly black horizontal regions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Abrupt changes in overall luminance between successive frames.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Irregular horizontal boundaries with fragmented and broken edges.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Short horizontal white, gray, and dark dropout streaks.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Dense horizontal interference in selected active regions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Low overall color saturation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Occasional subtle pink/magenta chromatic tint during bright events.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Occasional subtle dark-green tint during dark events.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Soft, degraded, low-detail signal appearance.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Stable outer frame boundaries without global frame rotation or aggressive vertical warping.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The effect must remain predominantly monochrome.\
Do not introduce strong rainbow coloration, dense RGB speckle noise, large diagonal shears, or unrelated chromatic streaks.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 4. Dedicated Engine Architecture\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Create:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Sync Collapse & Luma Dropout Engine
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Inside VHS DAMAGE LAB, organize the implementation into three coordinated subsystems.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 A. Horizontal Sync Collapse System\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 This is the primary subsystem.\
Generate irregular horizontal bands that span the frame and change their vertical positions, thicknesses, brightness, and fragmentation over time.\
Required behavior:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Multiple horizontal bands distributed across the frame.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Variable band height and spacing.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Bright, gray, and dark alternating regions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Irregular band boundaries.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Row-dependent horizontal displacement.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Broken horizontal segments.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Localized horizontal tearing.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Temporal changes in band structure.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Full-frame coverage capability.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Use row-based and band-based procedural functions.\
For each row or band, calculate deterministic values from its vertical coordinate, temporal state, and user seed.\
Support horizontal resampling using a row-dependent displacement:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 sourceX = x - horizontalOffset(y, time, seed)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
The displacement should be adjustable and should not become an uncontrolled global geometric distortion.\
Do not force every band to have identical thickness, brightness, or spacing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 B. Luma Instability & Flash Pulse System\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement an independent luminance-instability subsystem.\
The reference contains an important abrupt transition from very dark frames to a bright frame and back to dark frames.\
Required behavior:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Frame-level luminance pulses.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Abrupt bright and dark transitions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Independent local luminance fluctuations inside horizontal bands.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Bright white/gray flashes.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Deep dark signal-collapse regions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Irregular pulse timing.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Optional subtle luminance modulation within individual bands.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The engine must support both:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Procedural automatic pulse generation.\
{\listtext	2.	}User-controlled event timing or keyframe-driven intensity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Do not hardcode the bright event to a specific timestamp such as 00:00.250. That timestamp is an observation from this particular reference, not a universal timing rule.\
Expose separate controls for global luminance instability and local band luminance variation.\
Avoid simply changing the exposure of the entire image. The reference requires luminance variation coordinated with horizontal signal bands.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 C. Fine Dropout & Horizontal Streak System\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 Generate short horizontal bright and dark streaks.\
Required behavior:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Short horizontal segments.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Variable segment length.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Variable brightness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Irregular spacing.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Randomized row placement.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Broken and fragmented segments.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Bright white/gray streaks.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Dark interruptions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Temporal appearance and disappearance.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Higher concentration in selected active bands.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The streaks must remain visually distinct from ordinary scanlines.\
Do not turn them into continuous full-width horizontal lines.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 5. Subtle Chromatic Variation\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement a restrained optional chromatic-tint subsystem.\
The reference is primarily grayscale, with limited color variation.\
Support:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Subtle pink/magenta tint.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Subtle dark-green tint.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Optional slight RGB channel offset.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Low-intensity chromatic bleeding.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Chromatic variation should be independently controllable and must not dominate the effect.\
Allow the tint to vary between temporal events without forcing a fixed sequence.\
Do not add strong rainbow gradients or saturated colored noise.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 6. Temporal Event Architecture\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 The temporal behavior is critical.\
The reference demonstrates abrupt, unstable changes rather than a clearly periodic animation.\
Implement a deterministic event system with:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Event intensity.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Event duration.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Event transition sharpness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Bright-event probability.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Dark-event probability.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Event timing.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Recovery behavior.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Temporal randomness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}User seed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Support three modes:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Automatic Procedural Mode:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  Generate irregular bright and dark collapse events using deterministic temporal logic.\

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Manual / Keyframed Mode:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  Allow users to control event intensity and timing through After Effects animation.\

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Frozen Mode:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  Freeze the temporal state for a stable still-frame result.\
Use the actual After Effects composition time and frame information.\
The same seed, frame, and parameters must produce identical results.\
Do not use wall-clock time, uncontrolled global random state, or thread-dependent random generation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

