\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 9. Processing Pipeline\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Use a coordinated processing sequence:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Read and correctly interpret the input frame.\
{\listtext	2.	}Evaluate the current temporal event state.\
{\listtext	3.	}Generate horizontal band geometry and row-dependent displacement.\
{\listtext	4.	}Apply horizontal sync collapse and band luminance structure.\
{\listtext	5.	}Apply global and local luminance instability.\
{\listtext	6.	}Generate and composite fine horizontal dropout streaks.\
{\listtext	7.	}Apply subtle chromatic variations.\
{\listtext	8.	}Perform final compositing and output conversion.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The implementation may adapt this sequence to the existing VHSart architecture where technically necessary, but the three primary subsystems must remain independently controllable.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 10. Input and Generated-Signal Modes\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Provide two operating modes:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Apply Over Original:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  Apply horizontal synchronization collapse and luminance damage to the input footage while retaining adjustable source visibility.\

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Generated Signal:
